+# Feature Specification: Equipment Availability
+
+**Feature Branch**: `002-equipment-availability`
+**Created**: 2026-10-22
+**Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Add `availability(query)` to the rental service, with `query = { start, end, kind? }`, returning the sorted ids of the equipment of that kind (any kind when none given) that is free for the whole period.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*
+
+### User Story 1 - See what can still be rented (Priority: P1)
+
+Desk staff give a period, and optionally a kind (board or sail), and see at a glance which items can be rented for the whole of it.
+
+**Independent Test**: Register two boards and a sail, book one board for part of a period, ask for availability of that period: the booked board is absent.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** registered equipment and no bookings, **When** asking for a period without a kind, **Then** all equipment ids are returned, sorted.
+2. **Given** a kind, **When** asking, **Then** only ids of that kind are returned.
+3. **Given** a booking overlapping any part of the period, **When** asking, **Then** that item is not returned.
+4. **Given** a booking ending exactly when the period starts (or starting exactly when it ends), **When** asking, **Then** the item is returned.
+5. **Given** no equipment is free, or none is registered, **When** asking, **Then** an empty list is returned.
+
+### Edge Cases
+
+- A period that is not midnight UTC, empty, reversed, or not valid ISO-8601 UTC is rejected, as for quote/book.
+- A kind other than board/sail is rejected; an omitted (undefined) kind means any kind.
+- Asking never changes any state.
+
+## Requirements *(mandatory)*
+
+### Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: System MUST provide `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returning an array of equipment ids.
+- **FR-002**: An item is returned only if it has no booking overlapping the period (same overlap rule as booking; touching boundaries do not overlap).
+- **FR-003**: When `kind` is given only items of that kind are considered; otherwise all items.
+- **FR-004**: Ids MUST be returned sorted in ascending order.
+- **FR-005**: Period rules MUST match quote/book; invalid periods and invalid kinds MUST be rejected with an error.
+- **FR-006**: The operation MUST NOT modify bookings or equipment.
+
+### Key Entities
+
+- **Availability query**: start, end, optional kind.
+
+## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*
+
+- **SC-001**: An id is listed if and only if booking that item for the same period would succeed.
+- **SC-002**: The result is always sorted and contains no duplicates.
+- **SC-003**: Every invalid query is refused.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- Sorting is plain ascending string order of ids.
+- Only periods are checked; price and past dates are not restricted.
